---
import ProseLayout from "../layouts/ProseLayout.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../lib/schema";
import { SITE } from "../consts";

const siteUrl = Astro.site ?? new URL("https://wishfy.ai");
const url = "/about/";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: "Waseem Mansha",
  jobTitle: "Founder",
  worksFor: { "@id": new URL("/#organization", siteUrl).toString() },
  url: new URL(url, siteUrl).toString(),
};

const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbSchema(siteUrl, [
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "About", url },
  ]),
  personSchema,
];
---

<ProseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Wishfy is an AI-native search visibility consultancy. We make businesses the obvious answer in Google, ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Wishfy is an AI-native search visibility consultancy and product studio. We
    help businesses get found, get cited, and get chosen — across every kind
    of search that matters today.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>SEO</strong> — Google, Bing, and traditional organic search</li>
    <li><strong>GEO</strong> — Generative Engine Optimization for ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Perplexity</li>
    <li><strong>AEO</strong> — Answer Engine Optimization for featured snippets, "People Also Ask", and voice</li>
    <li><strong>Build services</strong> — when strategy isn't enough, we ship the website, content, schema, and code</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We are not a "rankings vendor." We are the team that makes a business <em>the
    obvious answer</em> when its customers ask anyone — human or machine — for a
    recommendation.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we exist</h2>
  <p>
    The search landscape has fractured. A brand can no longer rank #1 on Google
    and call it a day. Customers ask ChatGPT. They ask Claude. They ask
    Perplexity. They ask Siri. They scroll TikTok search. Each surface has its
    own grammar, and most agencies are still pretending it's 2018.
  </p>
  <p>Wishfy is built for what search actually is in 2026.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Discovery call (20 min, free).</strong> We learn the business, the goals, the timeline, and the budget tier.</li>
    <li><strong>Written proposal in one business day.</strong> Scope, deliverables, price band, and a kickoff date.</li>
    <li><strong>Visible work.</strong> You see the Paperclip board filtered to your project — no black-box retainers.</li>
    <li><strong>30-day check-ins.</strong> Even on retainers. We say what worked, what didn't, and what's next.</li>
    <li><strong>Exit-friendly.</strong> You own your content, your schema, your site, your data. We never hold artifacts hostage.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Specificity over generality.</strong> Every recommendation must be actionable in under a week.</li>
    <li><strong>Honesty over optimism.</strong> If something will take 90 days, we say 90 days. We don't sell hope.</li>
    <li><strong>Show the work.</strong> Every claim cites a source. Every output is reproducible.</li>
    <li><strong>Outcomes over outputs.</strong> "Twelve blog posts" isn't a deliverable. "Twelve posts that earned four featured snippets and two LLM citations" is.</li>
    <li><strong>AI-augmented, human-accountable.</strong> Agents draft. Humans approve. Waseem signs off on anything that touches a client's brand voice or a public commitment.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The founder</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Waseem Mansha</strong> founded Wishfy in Amsterdam after more than
    a decade of building products and growth programs across SaaS, e-commerce,
    and AI tooling. He works directly on every engagement until it's stable,
    then hands it to the team — never the reverse. Reach him at
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
